ontent":"mode"},"245":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-243","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"AgentMode"},"246":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-244","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"Mode for this run only"},"247":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-245","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"signal"},"248":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-246","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"AbortSignal"},"249":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-247","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"Abort the run"},"250":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-248","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"thinking"},"251":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-249","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"{ budgetTokens } | false"},"252":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-250","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"Extended thinking for this run"},"253":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-251","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"tools"},"254":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-252","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"{ allow?, deny? }"},"255":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-253","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"Narrow the tools for this run: names, * globs (\"docs__*\" is every tool of MCP server docs) or regexes"},"256":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-254","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentruntask-opts","content":"Returns { output, usage, trace, background?, traceId?, status? }; status is \"stopped\" when session.stop() ended the run (absent means completed); traceId is the turn's trace when telemetry is on, and also rides on that turn's stream:start, cost:update and done events. The same options apply to session.send(input, opts?)."},"257":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-255","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Agent methods: run, session, on, setMode, mcp, models, workflow, workflows, capabilities."},"258":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-256","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Session methods: on, send, setMode, getMode, saveWorkflow, runWorkflow, generateWorkflow, answer, approve, reject, editTodo, stop, cancel, history, close."},"259":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-257","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"session.setMode(mode) sets that session's mode only; a session that never set one follows agent.setMode."},"260":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-258","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"session.stop() aborts the run in flight and keeps the session: its pending approvals are rejected and questions settle unanswered (approval:resolved / elicitation:resolved), that send resolves with result.status: \"stopped\" and the text written so far as output (done carries status: \"stopped\" too; only real failures reject), and the next send works. session.cancel() ends the session for good."},"261":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-259","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"session.generateWorkflow(task) drafts a WorkflowGraph with the session's model without running it."},"262":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-260","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"session.editTodo(id, textOrPatch) takes new text or { text?, status? }."},"263":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-261","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"MCP: servers, tools, resources, connect, disconnect, reload, call, completeAuth, expose. HTTP servers use the official MCP SDK client (streamable HTTP with SSE fallback) and the full authorization spec out of the box: WWW-Authenticate → protected-resource metadata → authorization-server metadata (oauth-authorization-server/openid-configuration) → dynamic client registration → PKCE on a loopback redirect → token refresh, persisted under .agentkit/mcp-auth/. Configure per server via auth (clientId, scopes, redirectUrl, store, onAuthorize, callback) or set auth: false for static headers only."},"264":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-262","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Models: agent.models.list/add/remove/setDefault/test/usage/refresh — add requires provider.userConfigurable: true; refresh syncs Ollama tags via listOllamaModels()."},"265":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-263","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Workflows: agent.workflow(name), agent.workflows.run/list/get/delete, session.runWorkflow(id, input?) (approvals in that session), workflowInputKeys(def) (the {{input.key}} names a workflow reads). AI steps run on the model of the session or run that started them (session.runWorkflow(id, input, { model }), or the send's model for runs from chat); agent.workflows.run uses the current default; a step's own model wins."},"266":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-264","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"RAG (when rag is configured): agent.rag.ingest(docs), agent.rag.retrieve(query, topK?), agent.rag.remove(docId), agent.rag.count(), agent.rag.sources() (documents ingested in this process: { id, title?, chunks, metadata? }, title from metadata.title)."},"267":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-265","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Helpers: detectProviders(env?) lists every built-in provider with an API key set ({ id, provider, model, apiKey }, in the order Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Mistral, Groq, Nebius, NVIDIA). createRuleProvider(rules, { fallback? }) is an offline model that answers by matching the conversation (see Providers)."},"268":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-266","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Lifecycle: agent.close() disconnects MCP servers and closes memory/tool-cache stores (idempotent)."},"269":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-267","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Providers implementing embed(text) expose embeddings for retrieval and similarity checks (e.g. dynamic workflow repeat detection)."},"270":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-268","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#agentsessionopts--agentmcp","content":"Large tool results are stored as compact handles; the model can call __expand_result to fetch the full payload."},"271":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-269","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#streaming-a-run-agentstream--streamtoconsole","content":"agent.stream(task, opts?) and session.stream(input, opts?) return an AgentStream — an async-iterable of every AgentEvent, plus a result promise. The iterator ends on the terminal done/error event; stream.cancel() unsubscribes (and cancels the underlying run for a session.stream()). streamToConsole(stream, opts?) renders a live run to the terminal (TTY/NO_COLOR-aware). attachConsole(sessionOrAgent, { events?, color?, out? }) prints the same view for everything a session or agent emits and returns a detach function."},"272":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-270","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#streaming-a-run-agentstream--streamtoconsole","content":"This is the pull-based counterpart to the push-based agent.on(...) bus; both can be used together. See Core concepts → Streaming."},"273":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-271","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"Where subagents are call-and-return delegation, a handoff transfers control — a triage agent routes the conversation to a specialist that takes over (and may hand off again). Each agent gets generated transfer_to_<name> tools; the team runs on a shared EventBus and emits the agent:handoff event."},"274":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-272","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"Field (HandoffAgentDef)"},"275":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-273","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"Type"},"276":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-274","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"Description"},"277":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-275","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"name"},"278":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-276","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"string"},"279":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-277","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"Unique agent id (lowercase letters, digits, underscores)"},"280":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-278","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"description"},"281":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-279","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"string"},"282":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-280","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"Shown in other agents' transfer_to_<name> tool — say when to route here"},"283":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-281","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"system / model / tools"},"284":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-282","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"—"},"285":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-283","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#multi-agent-handoffs-createhandoffteam","content":"Per-agent prompt, model, and tools"},"286":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-284","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"