,"content":"Core concepts","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts"},"365":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-0","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts","content":"Agent, session, events, and modes"},"366":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-1","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#two-levels","content":"Two levels"},"367":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-2","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#agent","content":"Agent"},"368":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-3","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#models","content":"Models"},"369":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-4","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#session","content":"Session"},"370":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-5","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#streaming-a-run","content":"Streaming a run"},"371":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-6","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#events","content":"Events"},"372":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-7","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#harness-replay","content":"Harness replay"},"373":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-8","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"Modes"},"374":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-9","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#multi-agent","content":"Multi-agent"},"375":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-10","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#evaluation","content":"Evaluation"},"376":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-11","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/core-concepts#resilience","content":"Resilience"},"377":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-12","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#two-levels","content":"AgentKit has a configured level and a compositional one. createAgent(config) is the first: configuration in, agent out. Under it is a plugin kernel where every part of a turn is a service you can replace or an event you can intercept — see Extending AgentKit. The concepts below describe the configured level; both run the same tool pipeline and the same session log."},"378":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-13","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#agent","content":"createAgent(config) returns an object with run, session, on, mcp, models, workflow, and related helpers. Configuration is validated at construction time with Zod."},"379":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-14","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#models","content":"When provider.registry or userConfigurable is set, agent.models manages a hot-swappable registry. The active model resolves on every send() — see Models & switching."},"380":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-15","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#session","content":"agent.session() is interactive: send, stream, on, approve, answer, cancel, close, setMode. Use this for chat UIs and long-running work with human gates. agent.setMode() applies to subsequent run() calls on the same agent instance."},"381":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-16","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#session","content":"Switching mode emits mode:changed on the event bus (and over the wire when using @agentkit/server)."},"382":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-17","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#streaming-a-run","content":"on() is push-based (one bus, many subscribers — ideal for UIs and @agentkit/server fan-out). agent.stream(task) and session.stream(input) are the pull-based counterpart over the same events: they start a run and return an async iterable plus a typed result promise. Both can be used together."},"383":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-18","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#streaming-a-run","content":"The iterator ends on the terminal done/error event; on failure stream.result rejects. Breaking out of the loop (or stream.cancel()) unsubscribes — on a session.stream(), cancel() also cancels the underlying run. For a ready-made terminal view, pass the stream to streamToConsole(...)."},"384":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-19","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#streaming-a-run","content":"Events are shared across all sessions of the same agent (one bus per agent). For isolation between concurrent conversations, create one agent per session."},"385":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-20","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#events","content":"All subsystems publish to one typed event bus. Subscribe with agent.on or session.on. The same events map to AG-UI on the wire via @agentkit/server."},"386":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-21","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#events","content":"Notable groups: stream:* and thinking:* for model output, tool:* / mcp:tool:* for tool calls, plan:* / todo:* for plan mode, cost:update and log for observability, mode:changed for runtime mode switches."},"387":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-22","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#harness-replay","content":"Record sessions with harness: { enabled: true, record: \"./sessions\" }, then replay on another model via API or the agentkit-replay CLI:"},"388":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-23","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#harness-replay","content":"See Harness and examples/cli-agent."},"389":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-24","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"Mode"},"390":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-25","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"Behavior"},"391":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-26","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"direct"},"392":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-27","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"Task in, result out"},"393":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-28","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"ask"},"394":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-29","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"Conversational, clarifies before acting"},"395":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-30","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"plan"},"396":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-31","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"Plan and todos before execution"},"397":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-32","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"background"},"398":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-33","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#modes","content":"Fire and forget with done event"},"399":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-34","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#multi-agent","content":"Two composition styles. Subagents (subagents config, agentAsTool) are delegation: the parent calls an agent_<name> tool, the subagent runs in isolation, and its result returns to the parent. Handoffs (createHandoffTeam) are a control transfer: a triage agent routes the conversation to a specialist via a transfer_to_<name> tool, and that specialist takes over and answers (and may hand off again). Handoffs emit agent:handoff and run on a shared event bus, so streaming and the wire observe them. See handoffs in the reference."},"400":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-35","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#evaluation","content":"evaluate(target, cases) runs a suite through an agent and returns a pass/fail EvalReport — assert behaviour (output, tool use, cost) like any other test, composing with vitest/jest. Built-in scorers cover text matching, tool calls, cost/step ceilings, structured-output schemas, and custom logic. See evaluating agents."},"401":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-36","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#resilience","content":"Two opt-in guards on a run. budget sets per-run ceilings (maxCostUsd, maxTokens, maxToolCalls, maxDurationMs) and aborts with a BudgetExceededError when crossed. retry automatically retries transient provider failures (network blips, 429, 5xx, 529) with exponential backoff — only before any token is streamed, so output is never duplicated. See budget/retry in the reference."},"402":{"id":"/docs/core-concepts-37","page_id":"/docs/core-concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/core-concepts#resilience","content":"See Configuration reference for the full event list."},"403":{"id":"/docs/getting-started","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting started","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started"},"404":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"Install AgentKit and run your first agent"},"405":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Getting started"},"406":{"id":"/docs/getti