ently without the author scheduling anything."],[1684,"A malformed settings file fails loudly at load. Silently ignoring it would mean a typo'd JSON file makes a policy quietly stop applying — the failure mode worth the least tolerance."],[1471,"A minimal v1"],[2086,"a mode changes the visible tool set and the prompt, per agent"],[1654,"A model that can only make one tool call per step spends a step filtering a list, another chaining a result into the next call, and a third summarising. Code Mode collapses that: every visible tool becomes await tools.<name>(args) inside a single run_code program."],[1474,"A multi-session coding agent runs in a terminal, a desktop shell or a web chat without owning an editor. It keeps many conversations, each with its own history and workspace; reads, edits, greps and runs commands in a project root behind approvals and a sandbox; delegates to subagents; persists sessions across restarts and reconnects clients to work in flight."],[1895,"A narrower world for one agent"],[1616,"A one-shot shell loses everything between calls: a cd, an activated virtualenv, an SSH session, a REPL. That is the right default — reproducible and cheap — which is exactly why the stateful case needs its own seam rather than a flag on the stateless one."],[1568,"A patch targets a row by id and applies in order, so a deployment tunes a composition it does not own:"],[2272,"A pending call renders as generic, terminal, or diff. A completed call adds search and web:"],[1859,"A plan the UI can render"],[2061,"A plugin may declare a schema. Zod works directly, and so does anything else with a parse:"],[2237,"A plugin that needs durable state extends the event map and says how the model should see it:"],[1528,"A policy listener, so no tool can forget it"],[2130,"A policy plugin, end to end"],[1738,"a prompt section"],[1770,"A prompt section lists the catalogue: every tool with a short description, or, past 30\ndeferred tools, one line per MCP server or category with a count and example names.\nctx.tools.defer(predicate) is the registry primitive underneath; a realm inherits its\nparent's deferrals and cannot undo them. createAgent has the same behaviour built in as\ntoolSearch."],[1554,"A published CLI. mini-harness is the reference; promoting it to a package with the settings-files convention is packaging, not runtime work."],[2101,"a read-only researcher in its own tool realm, delegated to through one task tool"],[1510,"A registry with its own waterfall, no model turn"],[1537,"A seam and a tool; bring a provider"],[1701,"A seam rather than scattered process.env reads, for three reasons: a hosted deployment usually has a vault instead of an environment, a missing key should be one clear failure rather than an adapter-specific one, and a value that never becomes a plain property is much harder to log by accident."],[762,"A search_tools tool: the model asks for what it needs (\"post to slack\", \"github\") and\nthe best matches become callable on its next step, with their full definitions."],[1566,"A sequence of runtime.plugin() calls is a program. You can read it, but you cannot address a line of it from outside — so a consumer who wants one row changed has to fork the package that published it."],[2059,"A service is read through the reader's own context, so a registration made inside a service method belongs to the calling plugin:"],[2036,"A service published at ctx.<name> is reachable by every plugin in the tree. Augment the Services interface to type it:"],[1570,"A set or replace against a row that is not there throws rather than silently doing nothing. A composition you cannot trust to have applied is worse than no composition at all — a typo in an id should not become a security policy that quietly stopped applying. (remove of an absent id is a no-op, since \"make sure this is gone\" is already satisfied.)"],[1022,"A single run can use another model without changing the default: session.send(input, { model: \"fast\" }) takes a registry id or a provider/model id."],[1434,"A store listens to the session only while something is subscribed. See Streaming & wire protocol for endpoints and event types."],[1144,"A store takes a ClientSession (from connect() or hub.session(id)) or a bare event source ({ onAny }, e.g. streamAll()): without a session the state follows the events and the actions reject with \"Session not connected\"."],[2066,"A terminal coding agent built only from public plugin APIs"],[1794,"A tool calls ctx.fs.readFile(path); it does not know whether that lands on a local disk, a container, or an object store. That indirection is the point — a tool written for a laptop runs unmodified against a remote sandbox."],[1745,"A tool can say what it does to the world:"],[1823,"A tool has a value, a rendering and a card"],[2257,"A tool has four audiences and they want different things. The runtime validates arguments, code consumes a canonical value, the model reads prose, and a UI renders a card. Collapsing those into one string is what makes tool output either unusable by code or unreadable by the model."],[2350,"a tool node naming a tool the agent does not have becomes an AI node;"],[2262,"A tool that already publishes its own model-facing schema — an MCP server, for instance — passes it as jsonSchema and owns its own validation, rather than having one derived from a placeholder Zod type."],[1937,"a tools/execute listener"],[1939,"a tools/post-execute listener"],[1933,"a tools/pre-execute listener, or approvalPolicy by annotation"],[2098,"a UI that imports no tool, and gets new tools' cards for free"],[2260,"A value that describes a failure — a command's non-zero exit — can still be returned rather than thrown: output.isError(args, value) marks the result isError while the model reads the rendered value as usual. bashTool does this for a non-zero exit, so the session log, UIs, workflows and Code Mode see the command fail."],[633,"A: structured run()"],[249,"Abort the run"],[248,"AbortSignal"],[190,"access"],[1406,"Actions"],[2151,"adapter registration and streaming"],[749,"Adaptive TOON/JSON/CSV encoding and context compaction"],[1253,"Add (BYOK) or remove a model (when userConfigurable)"],[1924,"add a capability"],[1964,"add a human command that costs no model turn"],[540,"Add BYOK model"],[1946,"add durable state that survives a reload"],[1940,"add model-facing context"],[1556,"Add your own tools with defineHarnessTool, your own prompt sections, and a tools/ask responder that talks to your UI. Everything above runs on the mock provider for tests, and dumpConfig-style printing with describeBundle shows anyone what you shipped."],[2227,"Adding a durable fact"],[134,"Adds a handoff_to_human tool; calling it stops the run, emits handoff:request and sets result.handoff"],[502,"Adjust ../agentkit to your clone path, then:"],[495,"After editing AgentKit, rebuild and restart your app:"],[2037,"After that, ctx.tools is typed everywhere, with no registry lookup and no casts."],[2355,"After workflow:save:prompt, persist via session:"],[367,"Agent"],[1244,"Agent capability flags + enriched models block"],[750,"Agent config"],[257,"Agent methods: run, session, on, setMode, mcp, models, workflow, workflows, capabilities."],[2125,"Agent runtime"],[2011,"Agent runtime — services, the turn, every extension point"],[2063,"Agent runtime — the services and extension points built on this"],[2248,"Agent runtime — where the log sits in a turn"],[1232,"Agent URLs in the examples: express-api serves page and agent on :8787 (agent at /api/agent), nextjs-chat mounts the agent in its own route (/api/agent on :3001), vanilla-js-ui serves both on :3001. Workflow UI uses :8788."],[365,"Agent, session, events, and modes"],[309,"agent:spawned, agent:done, agent:handoff"],[2385,"agent.capabilities().workflows is true when the store exists."],[845,"agent.mcp.tools() returns { name, serverId, description?, jsonSchema? } for each callable tool. Stdio servers take env: { KEY: \"value\" }, merged over the parent's environment. Leave a whole server out of one run with send(input, { tools: { deny: [\"<serverId>__*\"] } })."],[541,"agent.models.add({…})"],[529,"agent.models.list()"],[545,"agent.models.refresh()"],[533,"agent.models.setDefault(id)"],[537,"agent.models.test(id)"],[549,"agent.models.usage()"],[9,"agent.run(task, opts?)"],[380,"agent.session() is interactive: send, stream, on, approve, answer, cancel, close, setMode. Use this for chat UIs and long-running work with human gates. agent.setMode() applies to subsequent run() calls on the same agent instance."],[10,"agent.session(opts?) / agent.mcp"],[271,"agent.stream(task, opts?) and session.stream(input, opts?) return an AgentStream — an async-iterable of every AgentEvent, plus a result promise. The iterator ends on the terminal done/error event; stream.cancel() unsubscribes (and cancels the underlying run for a session.stream()). streamToConsole(stream, opts?) renders a live run to the terminal (TTY/NO_COLOR-aware). attachConsole(sessionOrAgent, { events?, color?, out? }) prints the same view for everything a session or agent emits and returns a detach function."],[2416,"agent.workflows.delete(id)"],[2410,"agent.workflows.get(id)"],[2408,"agent.workflows.list()"],[2412,"agent.workflows.run(id, input?)"],[2164,"agent/pre-step"],[2091,"agent/pre-step + context/compacted"],[2103,"agent/pre-step + tools/pre-execute"],[1729,"agent/pre-step, agent/request-error, context/compacted"],[2167,"agent/request"],[2170,"agent/request-error"],[2173,"agent/turn-stopping"],[1498,"AgentHandle.status, an inbox, followup(), steer(), cancel()"],[822,"AgentKit connects to external MCP servers at agent startup and merges their capabilities with your own Zod tools. MCP resources and source-classified tools feed read-only context; callable tools are namespaced as serverId__toolName and run through the same approval and reasoning loop as developer tools."],[377,"AgentKit has a configured level and a compositional one. createAgent(config) is the first: configuration in, agent out. Under it is a plugin kernel where every part of a turn is a service you can replace or an event you can intercept — see Extending AgentKit. The concepts below describe the configured level; both run the same tool pipeline and the same session log."],[427,"AgentKit headless agent runtime"],[414,"AgentKit is a headless TypeScript agent runtime. createAgent(config) validates config with Zod at construction. The engine ships providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Ollama, Gemini, Mistral, Groq, mock), tools, memory, MCP, workflows, and adaptive encoding."],[431,"AgentKit is a TypeScript agent runtime you import into existing projects. The engine runs on Node; any UI connects over the AG-UI wire."],[1475,"AgentKit is built for that shape at the plugin level, not the config level. createAgent and @agentkit/workspace still work for the simple case, but a product like this is a harness, and the spine is where a harness lives: createRuntime, agentRuntime(), and plugins on public extension points. Two examples prove it and are the right starting points:"],[418,"AgentKit ships a single-file guide written for AI coding assistants: every feature, the full config, events, the server/client/hook APIs and recipes. Install it into your project and your assistant builds with the SDK instead of hand-rolling servers, reconnects or approval queues:"],[605,"AgentKit Studio (studio)"],[797,"AgentKit surfaces runtime activity as typed AG-UI events rather than only stdout. Set logging.level to control log emissions from the agent shell, and subscribe to cost:update for per-turn token and cost estimates from the active provider."],[572,"AgentKit uses config over code at every level:"],[245,"AgentMode"],[1744,"AgentOptions"],[2214,"agentRuntime() deliberately mounts only the spine. These ship alongside it and are opt-in, because each one is a policy choice rather than a default:"],[2137,"agentRuntime() is six ctx.plugin() calls. Copy them and swap any one — nothing in it is privileged."],[2153,"agents"],[291,"Agents this one may transfer to (default: all others)"],[1496,"agents.create({ sessionId, model, mode, maxSteps, meta })"],[1519,"AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md in the prompt, read through the filesystem seam"],[2089,"AGENTS.md support in twelve lines"],[2393,"AI"],[2354,"AI nodes run without tools and do not stream stream:token; the session's done carries the last node's output, and each node's result is on workflow:step:done.output. With telemetry on, each run is one trace: a workflow.run root (generated: true, workflowId, workflowName) with the node spans under it, so it appears on the admin Workflows page."],[166,"AI-generated DAG workflows (unstable)"],[2409,"All definitions"],[800,"All events stream over SSE — see Streaming. No separate logging HTTP API."],[1194,"All hooks accept null while connecting and return empty state; a new session starts fresh. They take a ClientSession, a hub's hub.session(id), or a bare event source ({ onAny }, e.g. streamAll(); actions then reject)."],[385,"All subsystems publish to one typed event bus. Subscribe with agent.on or session.on. The same events map to AG-UI on the wire via @agentkit/server."],[1698,"allow"],[2184,"allow / deny / ask — the policy layer"],[1932,"allow / deny / ask on a tool call"],[1771,"allow wins over requireApproval. deny is registered as a guard, so no\nlater tools/pre-execute listener, however permissive, can lift it. A\ntool with delegates: true (call_tool, create_subagent) is passed\nthrough: the calls it makes are gated one by one. Questions go out on\ntools/ask; with no responder mounted, the call is declined."],[1507,"Allow, ask, deny by what a tool declares, plus shell-script hooks"],[1831,"Allow, ask, deny, by what a tool declares"],[199,"allowNetwork"],[1624,"allowParallelInProgress is required with no default: it changes the tool description the model reads, and a harness should state which working style it wants ra